  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>First step of the reaction involves reduction of nitro group to primary amine this can be done using Sn in presence of HCl or H<sub>2</sub>/Pd, but&nbsp;aromatic nitro compounds on reaction with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>LiAlH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>produces&nbsp;azo products.&nbsp;</p><p>Second step of the reaction involves diazotization, which involves the use of HNO<sub>2</sub>&nbsp;(or) NaNO<sub>2</sub>&nbsp;in HCl as the reagent ,Para toluene&nbsp;diazonium chloride formed is formed which on hydrolysis produces para-cresol.</p><p>And&nbsp;Para toluene&nbsp;diazonium chloride can be converted to benzoic acid by using&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>or</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi></math>&nbsp;followed by reaction with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>alkaline</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>medium</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/8b0c3af1-6c87-415e-a763-e4255ab8e6a0-image.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 256px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> may be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Pd</mi></mfrac></math>, ethanol;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>Sn</mi><mi>HCl</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> may be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>NaNO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>HCl</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></math>&nbsp;may be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> (i) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, (ii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>KOH</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#916;</mi></math> or (i) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>OH</mi></math>, (ii)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>KOH</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#916;</mi></math></p>",
